@startuml release-process
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
title CR-VAS-010: Release Process (CR -> Classify -> Impact -> Manifest -> Review -> Release)

(*) --> "Change Request"
"Change Request" --> "14-Item Checklist\n(problem, rationale, classification, impact, ...)"
"14-Item Checklist\n(problem, rationale, classification, impact, ...)" --> "Classify (Editorial .. Breaking .. Multi)"
"Classify (Editorial .. Breaking .. Multi)" --> "Impact Analysis Chain\nDefinition -> Invariants -> Qualification -> Schemas -> Tests -> Architecture -> Mappings -> Examples"
"Impact Analysis Chain\nDefinition -> Invariants -> Qualification -> Schemas -> Tests -> Architecture -> Mappings -> Examples" --> "Migration Class (M0..M4)"
"Migration Class (M0..M4)" --> "Manifest Composition\n{compatibility, changes, migration, dual_version}"
"Manifest Composition\n{compatibility, changes, migration, dual_version}" --> "Release Review"
"Release Review" --> [Block] "Patch for Qualification?" as BLK1
BLK1 --> [Yes] "Reject (SV-INV-003)" as REJ1
REJ1 --> (*)
"Release Review" --> [Block] "Cross-repo conflict?" as BLK2
BLK2 --> [Yes, no reconciliation] "Reject (SV-INV-006)" as REJ2
REJ2 --> (*)
"Release Review" --> [Pass] "Apply SemVer\n(major / minor / patch)"
"Apply SemVer\n(major / minor / patch)" --> "Publish Release Manifest"
"Publish Release Manifest" --> (*)

note right
  Per CR-VAS-010 §15: Compatibility values MUST be
  justified by the release review, not automatically
  inferred from the version number (SV-INV-002).
  Per CR-VAS-010 §17: The 14-item checklist is MANDATORY.
end note

@enduml
